{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>I have cleared out the consecrated portion.</b> This is the great terumah, which is consecrated (קדש), and it is one part in fifty — two per hundred. <br><b>From the house.</b> This is the challah given to the priests. <br><b>And I have also given it to the Levite.</b> This is the first tithe, and also to include the second tithe which he would set aside for himself. <br><b>To the stranger, the orphan, and the widow.</b> This is the poor man's tithe. And this is the order of the gifts: first he would set aside the great terumah for the priest, and it is called ראשית ('first'), as it is written (Deuteronomy 18:4): ״ראשית דגנך״; and afterwards he would set aside the first tithe for the Levite, as it is written (Numbers 18:21): ״ולבני לוי הנה נתתי כל מעשר בישראל״; and the Levite would set aside and give to the priest a tithe of the tithe; and afterwards the Israelite would set aside for himself the second tithe and go up to Jerusalem and eat it there — this is what is written (Deuteronomy 14:22): ״עשר תעשר את כל תבואת זרעך״ and so on, and ״ואכלת לפני ה' אלהיך מעשר״ — ״עשר תעשר״ speaks of two tithes: the first tithe and the second tithe. And afterwards, in the third year of the Sabbatical cycle, he would set aside the poor man's tithe and give it to the poor — this is what is said: לגר ליתום ולאלמנה. And concerning this it says here: ״כי תכלה לעשר את כל מעשר תבואתך בשנה השלישית שנת המעשר״ — the verse teaches you that in the third year of the Sabbatical cycle he must gather all his tithes from the years that have passed and give them, and now complete what was lacking. And thus the verse says (Deuteronomy 14:28): ״מקצה שלש שנים תוציא את כל מעשר תבואתך בשנה ההיא״ — and that is the third year, in which the poor man's tithe is set aside. And so it mentions here ״בשנה השלישית שנת המעשר״ — the year in which one sets aside a tithe anew, namely the poor man's tithe, for there is no second tithe in it as in the other years, since this poor man's tithe is in place of the second tithe. Therefore the verse says that after he has set aside his gifts — the terumah and the tithes — properly and in order, he should make the declaration and say: בערתי הקדש; and he should pray to HaShem, blessed be He, that He bless the land in its fruits and in the rain of His might. And he would not make the declaration until nothing remained in his possession of the obligations of the gifts that were fitting for him to give to the priests, the Levites, and the poor. And when does he make the declaration? On the last festival day of Pesach of the fourth year and of the seventh year, as it is said: ״כי תכלה לעשר״ — on the festival when all the tithes are completed, for many trees are gathered after Sukkot, so that those of the third year are completed by Pesach of the fourth year. And anyone who delayed his tithes — the verse required him to clear them out from the house; and this is what they said in tractate Avot: in the fourth year because of the poor man's tithe of the third year, and in the seventh year because of the poor man's tithe of the sixth year. And on the eve of the last festival day was the clearing out, and on the morrow he makes the declaration at minchah." "<b>According to all Your commandments which You commanded me.</b> That I set aside the gifts in their proper order. And the Sages, of blessed memory, interpreted: I did not change the order of their setting aside, for one may not give the first tithe precedence over terumah, nor the second tithe over the first, as it is written (Exodus 22:28): ״מלאתך ודמעך לא תאחר״.<br><b>I have not transgressed Your commandments,</b> that I did not set aside from one species for a different species, nor from detached produce for attached produce, nor from attached for detached, nor from the new crop for the old, nor from the old for the new.<br><b>Nor have I forgotten,</b> to mention Your name and Your kingship over it at the time of setting aside. And the rule is to mention in them the Name and the kingship, and they already said: any blessing in which there is no mention of the Name and the kingship is no blessing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:21.386083586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}